Source: debocker
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Matthew Shaw <mshaw.cx@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               dh-sequence-python3,
               pybuild-plugin-pyproject,
               python3-all,
               python3-setuptools
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/shawcx/debocker
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: debocker
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${python3:Depends},
         debian-archive-keyring,
         debootstrap,
         docker.io | docker-ce,
         ubuntu-keyring
Recommends: qemu-user-static
Description: build Docker images of old Ubuntu and Debian releases
 debocker runs debootstrap for an Ubuntu or Debian release, including
 end-of-life releases signed with removed archive keys, and imports the
 resulting root filesystem as a Docker image. qemu-user-static is needed
 to build images for a foreign architecture.
